\title{A Table of Nontrivial Integer Solutions}
\author{}
\date{}

\begin{document}

\maketitle

We consider the Diophantine equation
\begin{equation*}
y^{2}=(36n^{3}-19-12mn)^{2}-(2m)^{3}.
\end{equation*}

The trivial family is
\begin{equation*}
m=0,\qquad y=\pm(36n^{3}-19).
\end{equation*}

All solutions listed below are nontrivial, since \(m\neq 0\).

Each row represents two signed solutions, namely
\begin{equation*}
(n,m,y)=(n,m,\pm |y|).
\end{equation*}

Thus the table below gives \(30\) nontrivial \((n,m,|y|)\)-triples, corresponding to \(60\) signed nontrivial integer solutions.

